==Old Norse==

===Etymology 1===
From the same ultimate origin as {{m|non|sá}} and {{m|non|þat}}. Related to {{cog|ang|se}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|þes}}, {{cog|goh|dese}}, {{cog|en|this}} and {{cog|de|diese}}.

====Pronoun====
{{head|non|pronoun|cat2=demonstrative pronouns|neuter|þetta}}

# {{lb|non|demonstrative}} [[this]], [[that]] (referring to both persons and things)

=====Declension=====
{{non-decl-pron-sjá}}

===Etymology 2===
{{PIE root|non|sekʷ|id=see}}
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*sehwaną||to see}} (for cognates see there). Ultimately from {{der|non|ine-pro|*sekʷ-||to see, notice}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|non|séa|siá}}

====Verb====
{{non-verb}}

# to [[see]]

